    "justification": "The cumulative 1469-byte increase over v0.7.9 retains explicit route ownership, consent, authorization, independent external and persistent-change gates, fail-closed resume, credential lifecycle routing, and optional invocation guidance. Those cross-route decisions belong at startup; detailed protocols remain on demand. This version adds 16 bytes to the 7352-byte v0.19.2 gate: one Boundaries bullet states the host permission boundary (present the exact action for the user's grant before the first attempt; a denial is a stop, never a retry by another tool, flag or path), which only the always-loaded gate can reach for host-native work; three trims (a filler word, a clause its skill description already states, a list its route entry already enumerates) and the move of one credential-lifecycle composition sentence into its existing reference pay for it. No route condition, safety rule, authorization boundary, stop condition, or pinned anchor changes. The gate is 4 byte(s) below the 7372-byte maximum. No new host observation is claimed."
